d I thought that he probably  would and it's good to see that they  didn't drag that out as far as I'm  concerned the idea being what I said in  my last recap mr. robot is not his  father  he's an invention to be the father that  he didn't have and he says that here he  tells Elliott I'm not your father  which Elliott replies I know that's why  I created you you're the father I needed  not the father I had and this is  Christian Slater's chance to shine here  we got great performances by everyone in  the last episode but he wasn't front and  center in the way that the other  characters were and here we see that  this is a two-way street he wishes he  could undo what happened he wishes that  he hadn't kept this hidden because he  sees it was the wrong thing to do but  Elliott does have someone that he can  work with and trust in mr. robot at this  point and it feels like on some levels  it's the only way he could go on and  we'll get to that in a second  back at Angela's apartment Janus kicks  things into high gear because she's not  getting what she wants she decides that  this is the time to start killing Dom's  family one by one  and things feel pretty dire because we  know that Darlene can't actually find  Elliot she gets on the phone though and  no one's picking up we see the shot of  the phone with blood on it that we saw  in the trailers over and over again and  we realized that Dom had something up  her sleeve so it turns out that this guy  Deegan who we've seen in earlier  episodes and we thought that probably it  was maybe an exit plan for Dom she must  have helped him some way to get him out  of his charges where he is indebted to  her to protect her family from the dark  army when the time came  turns out he's really good at it and  what's more the conversation between him  and Janice is top-notch Janice has this  way of being really kind of creepy and  normal and just all business and this  guy is definitely the right person  because he seems like he mig